<text font-family="sans-serif" fill="black" x="230" y="230"
      font-size="16px" font-weight="bold">PC 11.047B Cardinal Astec</text>
<text font-family="sans-serif" font-size="14px" fill="black" x="230" y="248">(McCawley) Steele, Norman W; Seattle F Design, Apr 87, </text>
<text font-family="sans-serif" font-size="14px" fill="black" x="230" y="266">Original issue in March called this design "AZTEC" but</text>
<text font-family="sans-serif" font-size="14px" fill="black" x="230" y="284">in April there was a correction to "ASTEC".</text>
<text font-family="sans-serif" font-size="14px" fill="black"><tspan x="230" y="302">Angles for R.I. = 1.540</tspan>
<tspan x="230" y="320">65 facets + 4 girdles</tspan>
<tspan x="230" y="338">4-fold, mirror-image symmetry; 96 index</tspan>
<tspan x="230" y="356">L/W = 1.000  T/W = 0.722  U/W = 0.722</tspan>
<tspan x="230" y="374">P/W = 0.582 C/W = 0.171</tspan>
<tspan x="230" y="392">Vol/W&#179; = 0.364</tspan>
<tspan x="230" y="410">pc11047b.asc</tspan>
